      "content": "I'll read the original test and CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the code. The original file has dead code (methods with undefined generic `T`, unused helper methods, invalid syntax), and many unused imports. I'll write an improved, clean version that keeps only what's needed for the actual test.Now I'll compile-check the generated file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all dead code (unused methods with undefined generic `T`, invalid syntax, unused helper methods) and unused imports, while renaming the helper method to `assertCardinalityAndIsEmptyConsistency` and adding clearer inline comments that explain the two-pass structure and the per-iteration assertion intent."
